    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the problem is that there isn't really anything left to reevaluate. i've tried the therapy, the vacations, the career shifts... it's just the same cycle of debt and burnout every single time. it feels less like a 'rough patch' and more like this is just how my life is. i look at the next 30 years and i just see more of this. how am i supposed to keep \"fighting\" when there's nothing actually being won? it just feels like i'm running on a treadmill that's slowly crushing me.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
